<title>JAPAN: Japan 1996 crude oil imports data issued by MITI.</title>
<headline>Japan 1996 crude oil imports data issued by MITI.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of International Trade and Industry on Tuesday issued the following data on crude oil imports in 1996:</p>
<p> CRUDE OIL   (1,000 kl) (1,000 bbl) share%   yr/yr%</p>
<p> Iran	   25,971     163,358	9.9    +13.5</p>
<p> Saudi Arabia 52,289     328,898     19.8    + 0.6</p>
<p> Kuwait	 13,787	86,720	5.2    + 7.0</p>
<p> Neutral Zone 13,018	81,883	4.9    - 9.0</p>
<p> Qatar	  17,040     107,182	6.5    - 0.3</p>
<p> Oman	   14,739	92,708	5.6    -12.2</p>
<p> UAE	    71,144     447,496     27.0    - 1.1</p>
<p>(Middle East total:</p>
<p>		  210,686  1,324,215     80.0    + 0.4)</p>
<p> Malaysia	 5,076     31,928	1.9    - 7.3</p>
<p> Indonesia     18,086    113,761	6.9    -14.0</p>
<p> Vietnam	  4,579     28,802	1.7    - 8.2</p>
<p>(Southeast Asia total:</p>
<p>		   30,557    192,204     11.6    -22.0)</p>
<p> Mexico	   5,063     31,846	1.9    +13.4</p>
<p> Venezuela	   32	  201	0.0    -67.3</p>
<p>(South America total:</p>
<p>		    5,095     32,048	1.9    +11.7)</p>
<p> China	   13,239     83,273	5.0    - 2.3</p>
<p> Nigeria	  1,173	7,378	0.4    +28.5</p>
<p>(Africa total:</p>
<p>		    1,662     10,454	0.6    + 9.6)</p>
<p> Australia	1,867     11,743	0.7    -29.4</p>
<p> Others	     339	2,132	0.1   +205.4</p>
<p>OVERALL TOTAL 263,445  1,657,069    100.0    - 1.3</p>
<p>Note: Figures may not tally due to rounding off.</p>
